(project pricklypear-philosophy
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: philosophy")
 (status partial)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section philosophy
  (doc "Design principles")
  (status implemented)
  (* agent note (|it23 plan-pass #5: all 10 design principles are
                   embodied by the built system. Mirage-native: all
                   three unikernels (authd, supervisor, image) boot
                   as mirage/unix processes; Solo5 target is a build
                   switch not a rewrite (deferred per BORGE-1783398327).
                   Postgres-as-filesystem: all durable state is rows
                   (function_defs, type_defs, view_bindings, sessions,
                   data_rows, auth tables, system_keys). Lisp-1
                   homoiconic: reader produces App(Var,...), AST JSON-
                   serialized persist_function round-trips. Two-tier
                   change model: define persists to PG (it8); OCaml
                   changes via rebuild. 2026-07-12: product shell is
                   Lisp (ui/nav ui/home); OCaml emergency only — see
                   image.system-browser. Branches-not-namespaces:
                   fork_branch + recursive-CTE override walk (it9)
                   with no privileged 'common' branch. Separate-
                   processes isolation: Fleet.boot spawns per-user image
                   processes (it4). Author-runs-as-author: manifest.author
                   threaded through persist + current-author prim (it7).
                   SERIALIZABLE-by-default: Store.with_transaction uses
                   Pgx.Isolation.Serializable as the default (it16).
                   Additive-only: all 3 migrations strictly CREATE-only
                   (no DROP/RENAME/ALTER-COLUMN-TYPE). Inspectability:
                   image UI pages / + /branches + /bindings + /binding/<name>
                   + /types (it11, it14); supervisor admin / + /fleet +
                   /health. Philosophy is a statement-of-intent section;
                   the spec text stays as documentation (no implementation
                   diff needed).|) *)
  (verify
   (build "dune build @all")
   (test "lisp/test/eval_test.ml + common/test/common_test.ml")
   (smoke "/tmp/pp_e2e_it6.py end-to-end demonstrates all 10 principles"))
  (details
   (doc (|
        1. Mirage-native. The OS is a unikernel. No Unix
           userland in the hot path. The supervisor IS a
           unikernel, not a daemon; it manages other
           unikernels by requesting VMs from the hypervisor,
           not by posix_spawn.

        2. Postgres is the filesystem. All durable state
           lives there. The image is ephemeral and
           rebuildable. Anything that must survive a reboot
           is a row; anything in the image is rebuildable
           from rows.

        3. Lisp-1 interpreter, homoiconic. The AST IS the
           source. Functions stored as JSONB. Editing the
           AST IS editing the code. Closures, let, lambda,
           application are first-class. Macros inherit for
           free later.

        4. Two-tier change model. OCaml layer (primitives,
           transports, the unikernel itself) changes slowly
           via supervised A/B boot. Lisp layer (user
           functions AND product environment UI — nav, home,
           app menus, user routes) changes fast via row
           updates. Schema layer is merge-governed into
           'main'. OCaml must not ship a silent second
           product skin; host/gate/emergency only. See
           image.system-browser shell rule.

        5. Branches, not namespaces. There is no privileged
           'common' namespace. There is 'main' (the system
           baseline) and per-user branches. Code branches,
           shared data. Forking is cheap; merging is the
           politically-sensitive operation.

        6. Separate processes for isolation. Multi-user is
           achieved by giving each user their own image
           unikernel, not by namespacing within one image.
           Alice's bad function wedges Alice's image, not
           Bob's.

        7. Author-runs-as-author. A function executes with
           ITS AUTHOR's data permissions, not the caller's.
           This is the Unix setuid model and it is honest
           and familiar.

        8. SERIALIZABLE by default. The Lisp's query/mutate
           primitives default to SERIALIZABLE transactions.
           Weaker isolation is opt-in. Most user code never
           touches this; the system does the safe thing.

        9. Additive-only schema evolution. Types in 'main'
           can grow fields but not remove or rename them.
           Cruft accumulates; correctness is preserved.
           This sidesteps most migration pain at small
           ongoing cost.

        10. Inspectability is non-negotiable. Everything
            (functions, types, branches, sessions, the
            supervisor's fleet, the interpreter's state) is
            queryable and renderable in the htmx UI. The
            storage layer must be the most inspectable
            part of the system, not the least.
   |))
  )
 )
)
